---
title: Spheniscidae
---
# Spheniscidae

Spheniscidae holds all eighteen living penguin species, from the metre-tall
[[emperor-penguin]] to the little penguin of southern Australia. They take krill,
squid and small shoaling prey while submerged, propelling themselves through the
water with the flippers alone at speeds no other seabird sustains, the feet and
tail trailing as a rudder. Countershaded plumage conceals a penguin from above
against the dark of the water and from below against the light of the sky.
